      {
        "text": "Elizabeth “Lisa” Hernandez is an Illinois state representative and the Deputy Majority Leader. She was a senior policy advisor to Lt. Gov. Patrick Quinn and a Cicero public schools administrator for 17 years.",
        "cites": [1],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Elizabeth “Lisa” Hernandez is an Illinois state representative and the Deputy Majority Leader.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She was a senior policy advisor to Lt. Gov. Patrick Quinn and a Cicero public schools administrator for 17 years.",
            "cites": [1]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Hernandez backed a bill that passed the House to expand Latin American history instruction for public school students starting in the 2027-2028 school year. Her caucus page says 2026 laws she backed let people sending money abroad donate to the Illinois DREAM Fund, created a cosmetology apprenticeship program and require grocery chains with e-coupons to offer paper ones. In 2019, she co-sponsored a bill to ban for-profit immigrant detention centers in Illinois, stating they lacked oversight and specialized care.",
